  [OK] include/sbi/riscv_encoding.h:369-375  <global scope>
      CSR_SISELECT (0x150) and CSR_SIREG..CSR_SIREG6 (0x151-0x157) correctly define the architecturally-assigned S-mode indirect CSR alias numbers per the RISC-V privileged spec. These are the access mechanism through which spmpcfg is reached; the constants themselves are accurate and carry no mask/width assumptions.
  [RISK] include/sbi/riscv_encoding.h:153-168  <global scope>
      These PMP_R/W/X/A/L bit-position macros and PMP_SHIFT/PMP_COUNT/PMP_ADDR_MASK encode the legacy PMP 8-bit-per-entry layout. SPMP's spmpcfg uses a full SXLEN-bit-wide configuration field per entry with potentially different bit positions. If an SPMP implementation reuses these macros directly (e.g., PMP_R for spmpcfg bit 0), it would encode wrong permissions. The definitions themselves are correct for PMP; the risk is entirely from implicit reuse by future SPMP code that is not yet written.
  [RISK] include/sbi/sbi_hart.h:28-79  <enum sbi_hart_extensions>
